{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '190,203p;1619,1649p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '54,73p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '245,270p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '595,605p;630,670p;805,821p'\"","aggregated_output":"   190\t                           ([b enc] (String. ^bytes b ^String enc)))\n   191\t                    :cljs (fn [b] (.apply js/String.fromCharCode nil b))\n   192\t                    :cljd (fn [b] (dart:core/String.fromCharCodes b)))\n   193\t                 [1 2])\n   194\t           ['yin/def (primitive-entry\n   195\t                       'yin/def\n   196\t                       (fn [k v] {:effect :vm/store-put, :key k, :val v})\n   197\t                       :effectful [2] #{:vm/store-put})]\n   198\t           ['require (primitive-entry\n   199\t                       'require\n   200\t                       (fn [spec]\n   201\t                         (let [ns-sym (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec)]\n   202\t                           {:effect :module/require, :module ns-sym}))\n   203\t                       :effectful [1] #{:module/require})]])))\n  1619\t   cursor, and gap count belong to `dao.stream.observer`, which a host\n  1620\t   composes beside the VM rather than inside it.\"\n  1621\t  ([] (empty-state {}))\n  1622\t  ([opts]\n  1623\t   (let [installed-primitives (or (:primitives opts) primitives)\n  1624\t         installed-profiles (or (:primitive-profiles opts)\n  1625\t                                (into {} (keep (fn [[name _]]\n  1626\t                                                 (when-let [profile\n  1627\t                                                            (profile-of\n  1628\t                                                              installed-primitives\n  1629\t                                                              name)]\n  1630\t                                                   [name profile])))\n  1631\t                                      installed-primitives))\n  1632\t         standard-aliases (into {}\n  1633\t                                (filter\n  1634\t                                  (fn [[alias canonical]]\n  1635\t                                    (and (identical?\n  1636\t                                           (primitive-function\n  1637\t                                             (get installed-primitives alias))\n  1638\t                                           (primitive-function\n  1639\t                                             (get primitives alias)))\n  1640\t                                         (identical?\n  1641\t                                           (primitive-function\n  1642\t                                             (get installed-primitives canonical))\n  1643\t                                           (primitive-function\n  1644\t                                             (get primitives canonical))))))\n  1645\t                                primitive-canonical-names)\n  1646\t         canonical-names (merge standard-aliases\n  1647\t                                (:primitive-canonical-names opts))\n  1648\t         _ (assert-primitive-reverse-lookup-unique! installed-primitives\n  1649\t                                                    canonical-names)\n    54\t(defn resolve-var\n    55\t  \"Look up a variable name: env -> store -> primitives -> module registry.\n    56\t\n    57\t   The registry is a value supplied by the composition, not a global.\"\n    58\t  [env store primitives registry name]\n    59\t  (if-let [pair (find env name)]\n    60\t    (val pair)\n    61\t    (if-let [pair (find store name)]\n    62\t      (val pair)\n    63\t      (if-let [pair (find primitives name)]\n    64\t        (vm/primitive-function (val pair))\n    65\t        (if-let [resolved (when (namespace name)\n    66\t                            (module/resolve-module\n    67\t                              registry\n    68\t                              (symbol (str (namespace name)\n    69\t                                           \".\"\n    70\t                                           (clojure.core/name name)))))]\n    71\t          resolved\n    72\t          (fail (str \"Unable to resolve symbol: \" name \" in this context\")\n    73\t                {:symbol name}))))))\n   245\trestoration, and scheduling outside the stamp. UCF therefore versions the\n   246\t**complete execution contract**: the stamp names one published revision of\n   247\t\n   248\t- the tuple grammar of §7.3.2 — the mnemonic set, each mnemonic's tuple\n   249\t  arity and operand kinds, and the saturation/defaults table — plus the\n   250\t  §2.6 well-formedness rules and the resolved-interpretation\n   251\t  (last-value-wins) rule;\n   252\t- the §2.4 opcode table and the §4.2 transitions;\n   253\t- the resolution precedence of `resolve-var` (env → store → primitives →\n   254\t  modules);\n   255\t- the effect→outcome mapping of §3.3 and `engine/handle-effect`;\n   256\t- call restoration and the scheduler semantics of §3.5 — wait-entry shapes,\n   257\t  `check-wait-set`'s round order, `semantic-restore`.\n   258\t\n   259\t```clojure\n   260\t:yin.k/contract {:yin.code/contract \"v2\"    ; the revision above, by name\n   261\t                 :yin.k/version    0}       ; this envelope's own version\n   262\t```\n   263\t\n   264\tA resumer whose loader implements a different revision does not guess: it\n   265\treturns `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` (§7.9) *before* lowering. Adding an opcode,\n   266\tchanging a transition, or changing the resolution order is a new revision; a\n   267\tresumer on the old one cannot run code that observes the difference, and the\n   268\tstamp is how it finds out before lowering rather than at an unknown integer\n   269\tin `case`. Two revisions may be declared compatible only by a published\n   270\tstatement in `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4, never by an engine's own judgment.\n   595\t### 5.1 `:yin.ast/code` (the AST walker)\n   596\t\n   597\t```clojure\n   598\t{:format              :yin.ast/code\n   599\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   600\t :identity-fn         (fn [body] (jing/segment-key body))\n   601\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [root-id body] (jing/segment-matches? root-id\n   602\t                                                                  body))\n   603\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [body] (row-local-defect body))\n   604\t :validate-fn         (fn [tree] (yin.vm/validate-rows tree))\n   605\t :obligations-fn      (fn [tree] (free-name-occurrences tree))\n   630\t### 5.2 `:yin.semantic/code` (the semantic VM)\n   631\t\n   632\t```clojure\n   633\t{:format              :yin.semantic/code\n   634\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   635\t :identity-fn         jing/segment-key\n   636\t :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?\n   637\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   638\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   639\t :obligations-fn      semantic-free-names\n   640\t :definitions-fn      semantic-definitions\n   641\t :applications-fn     semantic-application-sites\n   642\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   643\t```\n   644\t\n   645\tPayload: the canonical positional instruction tuple vector (UCF section\n   646\t7.3.2), stored as the exact vector at its own `segment-key`; nothing\n   647\telse may hash there (UCF section 7.3.4). The identity is that address.\n   648\t`well-formed-vector?` is the section 7.5 grammar. `semantic-free-names`\n   649\tscans `:var` operands not bound by an enclosing closure's params, the\n   650\t`$code` query of section 7.7; `semantic-application-sites` scans the\n   651\tcall opcodes, including calls of imported names and of primitives\n   652\tthat receive a function argument; all three return the section 4.1\n   653\trecords. The linker module defines them, as B6 defined the two de\n   654\tBruijn scanners. The contract stamp is UCF's\n   655\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v2\"}`; a link request for this format carries the\n   656\tstamp, and the receiver's index is keyed per stamp (UCF section 7.3.3).\n   657\tLoading is `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`, which writes the address to the\n   658\timage and the alias column.\n   659\t\n   660\t### 5.3 `:yin.debruijn.code` (the stack VM)\n   661\t\n   662\t```clojure\n   663\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code\n   664\t :contract            \"b1\"\n   665\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash\n   666\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash v)))\n   667\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   668\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   669\t :obligations-fn      stack-free-names\n   670\t :definitions-fn      stack-definitions\n   805\tA `request` is plain data and nothing else. Its closed key set is\n   806\t`:yin.link/id`, `:yin.link/format`, `:yin.link/contract` (optional), and\n   807\texactly one of `:yin.link/name` or `:yin.link/identity`. The two\n   808\tadmissible shapes:\n   809\t\n   810\t```clojure\n   811\t;; by module name: the linker resolves the manifest (section 8)\n   812\t{:yin.link/id       [:t0 7]                  ; section 7.2, step 3\n   813\t :yin.link/format   :yin.debruijn.code\n   814\t :yin.link/contract \"b1\"\n   815\t :yin.link/name     'my.lib}\n   816\t\n   817\t;; by bare identity: B6's closed-image path, no manifest\n   818\t{:yin.link/id       [:t0 8]\n   819\t :yin.link/format   :yin.debruijn.code\n   820\t :yin.link/contract \"b1\"\n   821\t :yin.link/identity H}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-25 14:50:56 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 21:50:56 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nConsensus is reached on Rule R’s implementation direction, with one binding choice: **fold Change A into the versioned semantic cutover (Change B)**. Do not ship A as an erratum under the existing contracts. With that choice, no remaining P1 blocks implementation. This is design sign-off, not approval of code that has not yet been written.\n\nThe no-shadow proof is sound for execution. Both walker paths and the semantic, stack, and register variable instructions call `engine/resolve-var` ([ast_walker.cljc:379,628](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:379), [semantic.cljc:263](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:263), [stack.cljc:386](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:386), [register.cljc:390](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:390)). If it refuses `yin/def` *before* environment or store lookup, and the valid definition transition never resolves its operator, neither a restored binding nor a store entry can redirect a definition ([engine.cljc:54-73](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:54); [revision 2:28-38](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790344000000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-revision2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:28)). Direct store-get is not name resolution. The UCF `unsatisfied-names` helper is a static check with a supplied callback, **not** another `resolve-var` caller ([ucf.cljc:387-395](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:387)); Fable’s proof should say “every executing VM variable lookup,” not “every conformance check.”\n\nChange A cannot be an erratum. UCF explicitly includes resolver precedence in the stamped execution contract and says changing resolution order requires a new revision ([UCF:245-270](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:245)). The old precedence was specified behavior even though it enabled shadowing. Moreover, while `yin/def` remains a primitive, `empty-state` permits a composition-supplied primitive map, so “registry-only” lookup alone does not fix its meaning ([yin.vm.cljc:194-197,1623](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1623)). Fable explicitly offered folding A into B if the strict contract reading prevailed ([revision 2:51-55](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790344000000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-revision2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:51)). The coherent split is therefore two commits: atomic Rule R with `v3/v3/b2/r2`, then M2 guard removal.\n\nRequired stamps at linker fetch and every direct persistent-code loader are the right rule. Today fetch accepts an omitted contract and the direct semantic and stack loaders do not compare one ([linker.cljc:1184-1193](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:1184), [semantic.cljc:713-733](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:713), [stack.cljc:95-114](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:95)). An old-stamped image without definitions must fail by stamp, not by grammar. A caller falsely labelling byte-identical AST content `v3` is asserting a new interpretation; content bytes alone cannot prove its historical provenance. The stack loader’s absent validation is **not the only** current admission gap: the walker’s datom loader reconstructs an AST without whole-tree validation ([ast_walker.cljc:709-721](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:709)). The runtime refusal remains the security backstop; load-time refusal is still an implementation requirement.\n\nRemaining non-blocking corrections to carry into the implementation brief:\n\nP2 | [revision 2:24-26](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790344000000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-revision2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:24) | The proposed “no `assoc` into `:store` outside `yin.vm.engine`” lint is not a proof of one store-write function: `dao.await` merges into the store, the REPL writes fixed history keys, and the engine itself has resource and scheduler writes outside the proposed helper ([await.cljc:217-223](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/dao/await.cljc:217), [repl.cljc:598-603](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:598), [engine.cljc:404-425](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:404)). | Make the lint an exact allowlist/audit of state-construction writes; route all program writes through `engine/store-put` and assert scheduler update keys cannot be the reserved symbol. This strengthens the separate “store never holds the key” invariant; it is not needed for the no-shadow proof.\n\nP2 | [revision 2:46-47](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790344000000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-revision2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:46) | The producer list omits direct `vm/eval`, which creates AST datoms, and the expander’s transformer runner, which constructs and loads a bare row set ([ast_walker.cljc:765-778](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:765), [macro.cljc:723-732](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:723)). | Specify how these trusted fresh-code paths supply the required current contract; never silently assign it to externally supplied persistent datoms or rows. Include both paths in the Change B gate.\n\nP2 | [revision 2:55](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790344000000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-revision2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:55) | “Refused at load” does not describe a raw walker state stepped with directly supplied control; that path has no load event ([ast_walker.cljc:688-691](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:688)). | Test load-time refusal for loader inputs and transition-time refusal for raw control, including reserved store-get/update keys. Keep the old-stamped no-definition image and supplied-primitive cases in the gate.\n\nUCF frame encoding, continuation lower-time stamp refusal, and module-store snapshot lowering belong in M4 because UCF lift/lower is not implemented; local parked-during-definition resume belongs in Rule R now ([UCF status:1-5](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1), [revision 2:55-59](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790344000000-architect-yin-def-rule-r-revision2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:55)). The deferred UCF tests must remain explicit acceptance obligations, not be treated as passing today.\n\nVerdict: READY\nSign-off: GRANTED"}}
